<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore arrest 140 illegal immigrants.</title>
<headline>Singapore arrest 140 illegal immigrants.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore police said on Wednesday they had arrested 140 suspected illegal immigrants in a 30-hour operation.</p>
<p>A police spokesman said the suspects were from neighbouring countries but declined to name them.</p>
<p>&quot;More then 900 officers were involved in the 30-hour operation,&quot; a police statement said.</p>
<p>It said the operation was part of continuing efforts targetted at illegal immigrants in Singapore. Police sources said it was also linked to a recent spate of burglaries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3080)</p>
